  76: - args: `{ "client": "iolbox-gui/0.1.0" }`
  77: - result: `{ "supervisor": "0.1.0", "runtime": "debian-slim-12", "arch": "x86_64", "features": ["nvram","capture","i386"] }`
  78: 
  79: The `features` array always contains the base capabilities `nvram`, `capture`,
  80: `i386`. It additionally contains:
  81: - `natgw` â€” the runtime supports **nat** nodes (has `/dev/net/tun` and
  82:   passwordless `sudo`).
  83: - `mgmt` â€” the runtime supports **mgmt** nodes (the above plus a usable
  84:   management interface).
  85: 
  86: These are detected once at supervisor startup. Starting a `nat`/`mgmt` node on a
  87: runtime that did not advertise the matching feature returns an `unsupported`
  88: error (`"runtime does not support nat/mgmt nodes"`).
  89: 
  90: ### `image.list`
  91: - result: `{ "images": [ { "id","filename","class","arch","sha256","size" } ] }`
  92: 
  93: ### `image.register`
  94: Called after the provider has synced an image file into the runtime. Supervisor
  95: fingerprints + sniffs class/arch authoritatively.

